<body>

<header>
  <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue? — 为什么天空是蓝色的？</h1>
  <p>A bilingual guide for three audiences</p>
</header>

<!-- ═══════════════ 1. TODDLER ═══════════════ -->
<section>
  <div class="section-title">🌈 For a Toddler · 给幼儿（3 岁）</div>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="card en">
      <span class="lang-tag">English</span>
      <p>The sky is blue because the sun sends out <strong>rainbow colors</strong> when its light travels to Earth! All the colors—red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple—are in sunlight together.</p>
      <p>When that sunlight comes down, it bumps into tiny air particles, like invisible little dots floating around us. The <strong>blue light bounces around the most</strong>, like blue confetti flying everywhere. That's why when you look up, you see blue!</p>
      <p>At sunset, the light has to travel further, so the blue bounces away before it reaches your eyes, and you get to see red and orange instead. Pretty cool, right?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <span class="lang-tag">中文</span>
      <p>天空是蓝色的，因为太阳把<strong>彩虹般的颜色</strong>随着光线一起送到地球！所有颜色——红色、橙色、黄色、绿色、蓝色和紫色——都一起在阳光里。</p>
      <p>当阳光照射下来时，它会撞到微小的空气颗粒，就像浮在我们周围那些看不见的微小颗粒。<strong>蓝光到处弹来弹去</strong>，就像蓝色的彩纸碎片漫天飞舞。所以当你抬头看时，你看到的就是蓝色！</p>
      <p>日落时，光线要走的更远，所以蓝光在你看到之前就已经散开了，你看到的是红色和橙色。很酷吧？</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════ 2. HIGH SCHOOL ═══════════════ -->
<section>
  <div class="section-title">🎓 For a High School Student · 给高中生</div>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="card en">
      <span class="lang-tag">English</span>
      <p>The sky appears blue due to a phenomenon called <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>.</p>
      <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of all visible wavelengths of light—red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet. These wavelengths range from about <strong>380 nm (violet)</strong> to <strong>700 nm (red)</strong>.</p>
      <p>As sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules (mainly nitrogen and oxygen) that are much smaller than the wavelength of visible light. When this happens, shorter wavelengths (blue and violet) are scattered <strong>much more strongly</strong> than longer wavelengths (red and orange). The scattering intensity is proportional to <code>1/λ⁴</code>, meaning blue light (around 450 nm) is scattered roughly <strong>9–10 times more</strong> than red light (around 650 nm).</p>
      <p>So why don't we see violet, which has an even shorter wavelength? Two reasons:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>The Sun emits more blue light than violet light.</li>
        <li>Our eyes are more sensitive to blue, and some violet light is absorbed by the upper atmosphere.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The scattered blue light reaches our eyes from all directions, which is why the entire sky looks blue rather than just the area around the Sun. At sunrise and sunset, light travels through more atmosphere, so most blue is scattered away before it reaches us, leaving the reds and oranges we associate with golden hour.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <span class="lang-tag">中文</span>
      <p>天空呈现蓝色是由于一种叫做<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的现象。</p>
      <p>阳光看起来是白色的，但实际上它由所有可见光波长组成——红、橙、黄、绿、蓝、靛、紫。这些波长范围大约从 <strong>380 纳米（紫色）</strong> 到 <strong>700 纳米（红色）</strong>。</p>
      <p>当阳光进入地球大气层时，它与气态分子（主要是氮气和氧气）发生碰撞，这些分子比可见光波长小得多。这时，短波长（蓝色和紫色）比长波长（红色和橙色）<strong>散射得更强烈</strong>。散射强度与 <code>1/λ⁴</code> 成正比，这意味着蓝光（约 450 纳米）的散射大约是红光（约 650 纳米）的 <strong>9–10 倍</strong>。</p>
      <p>那我们为什么看不到紫色呢？紫色有更短的波长，原因有二：</p>
      <ol>
        <li>太阳发出的蓝光比紫光多。</li>
        <li>我们的眼睛对蓝光更敏感，而且部分紫光被高层大气吸收了。</li>
      </ol>
      <p>散射的蓝光从各个方向进入我们的眼睛，所以整个天空看起来都是蓝色的，而不仅仅是太阳周围的区域。在日出和日落时，光线穿过更多的大气，所以大部分蓝光在到达我们之前就被散射掉了，剩下我们看到的红色和橙色，也就是所谓的"金色时刻"。</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════ 3. PHYSICS PhD ═══════════════ -->
<section>
  <div class="section-title">🔬 For a Physics PhD · 给物理学博士生</div>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="card en">
      <span class="lang-tag">English</span>
      <p>The blue color of the sky is a consequence of <strong>elastic scattering of electromagnetic radiation by atmospheric molecules in the Rayleigh regime</strong>, where the scattering particles are small relative to the incident wavelength (<code>2πa/λ ≪ 1</code>).</p>

      <h3>Scattering Cross Section</h3>
      <p>For a single molecule with refractive index <em>n</em> and volume <em>V</em>, the Rayleigh scattering cross section is:</p>
      <div class="formula">σ = (8π³ / 3λ⁴) · [(n² − 1) / N]² · (6 + 3ρ) / (6 − ρ)</div>
      <p>where <em>N</em> is the molecular number density and <em>ρ</em> is the <strong>depolarization ratio</strong>, accounting for molecular anisotropy. The dominant <code>λ⁻⁴</code> dependence means that at 400 nm, scattering is ~9× stronger than at 700 nm.</p>

      <h3>Multiple Scattering and the Optically Thick Limit</h3>
      <p>Near the zenith, the atmosphere is optically thin for scattering (optical depth τ ≈ 0.1 at 550 nm), so single scattering is a reasonable approximation. However, at larger solar zenith angles—particularly near the horizon—the atmosphere becomes <strong>optically thick</strong>, and <strong>multiple scattering</strong> must be treated with a radiative transfer framework (e.g., the Schuster–Schwartzchild two-stream approximation or full Monte Carlo solutions to the RTE).</p>

      <h3>Why Blue, Not Violet?</h3>
      <p>The observed sky color is determined by the product of three factors:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Solar spectral radiance</strong> B(λ) — the AM1.5 spectrum peaks near 500 nm and drops significantly in the violet/UV.</li>
        <li><strong>Scattering phase function</strong> P(θ) — Rayleigh scattering is azimuthally symmetric with P(θ) ∝ 1 + cos²θ, which is forward/backward peaked and relatively isotropic at 90°.</li>
        <li><strong>Human cone sensitivity</strong> — the combined response of S, M, and L cones, weighted by the CIE 1931 color matching functions.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The net effect is that violet photons (~400 nm) are strongly scattered, but their low solar flux and poor S-cone sensitivity shift the perceived color toward <strong>blue</strong>.</p>

      <h3>Atmospheric Composition Dependence</h3>
      <p>The total scattering coefficient at sea level is dominated by N₂ (~78%) and O₂ (~21%), with minor contributions from Ar. The refractivity (<em>n</em> − 1) of air at STP is approximately <strong>2.9 × 10⁻⁴</strong>, yielding a scattering coefficient of roughly <strong>10⁻⁵ m⁻¹</strong> at 550 nm. This results in an <strong>effective scattering altitude</strong> on the order of 10–15 km, above which the sky progressively darkens (as observed from aircraft).</p>

      <h3>Beyond Rayleigh</h3>
      <p>At shorter wavelengths (UV), <strong>Mie scattering</strong> from aerosols and ozone absorption become relevant. At longer wavelengths (IR), the atmosphere becomes increasingly opaque due to vibrational absorption bands of H₂O and CO₂. The blue sky is thus a relatively narrow spectral window where Rayleigh scattering dominates and the atmosphere remains largely transmissive.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card cn">
      <span class="lang-tag">中文</span>
      <p>天空的蓝色是<strong>大气分子在瑞利 regime 下对电磁辐射的弹性散射</strong>的结果，其中散射粒子相对于入射波长很小（<code>2πa/λ ≪ 1</code>）。</p>

      <h3>散射截面</h3>
      <p>对于折射率为 <em>n</em>、体积为 <em>V</em> 的单个分子，瑞利散射截面为：</p>
      <div class="formula">σ = (8π³ / 3λ⁴) · [(n² − 1) / N]² · (6 + 3ρ) / (6 − ρ)</div>
      <p>其中 <em>N</em> 是分子数密度，<em>ρ</em> 是<strong>退偏比</strong>，用于考虑分子各向异性。主要的 <code>λ⁻⁴</code> 依赖关系意味着在 400 纳米处，散射强度约为 700 纳米处的 9 倍。</p>

      <h3>多次散射与光学厚极限</h3>
      <p>在天顶附近，大气在散射方面是光学薄的（550 纳米处光学深度 τ ≈ 0.1），所以单次散射是一个合理的近似。然而，在较大的太阳天顶角下——尤其是接近地平线时——大气变得<strong>光学厚</strong>，必须用辐射传输框架来处理<strong>多次散射</strong>（例如 Schuster-Schwartzchild 双流近似或辐射传输方程的完整蒙特卡洛解）。</p>

      <h3>为什么是蓝色，不是紫色？</h3>
      <p>观测到的天空颜色由以下三个因素的乘积决定：</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>太阳光谱辐亮度</strong> B(λ) —— AM1.5 光谱在约 500 纳米处达到峰值，在紫外/紫区域显著下降。</li>
        <li><strong>散射相函数</strong> P(θ) —— 瑞利散射在方位角上是对称的，P(θ) ∝ 1 + cos²θ，前向和后向散射较强，在 90° 处相对各向同性。</li>
        <li><strong>人眼锥细胞灵敏度</strong> —— S、M、L 三种锥细胞的综合响应，由 CIE 1931 色匹配函数加权。</li>
      </ol>
      <p>综合效果是：紫光光子（约 400 纳米）被强烈散射，但其太阳通量低且 S 型锥细胞灵敏度差，使感知颜色偏向<strong>蓝色</strong>。</p>

      <h3>大气成分依赖性</h3>
      <p>海平面处的总散射系数主要由 N₂（约 78%）和 O₂（约 21%）主导，氩气贡献较小。空气在标准温度和压力下的折射率 (<em>n</em> − 1) 约为 <strong>2.9 × 10⁻⁴</strong>，在 550 纳米处的散射系数约为 <strong>10⁻⁵ m⁻¹</strong>。这导致<strong>有效散射高度</strong>约为 10–15 公里，在此高度以上天空逐渐变暗（从飞机上可以观察到）。</p>

      <h3>超越瑞利散射</h3>
      <p>在较短波长（紫外线）下，气溶胶的<strong>米氏散射</strong>和臭氧吸收变得重要。在较长波长（红外）下，由于 H₂O 和 CO₂ 的振动吸收带，大气变得越来越不透明。因此，蓝色天空是一个相对狭窄的光谱窗口，在这个窗口中瑞利散射占主导地位，大气保持大部分透明。</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Toggle buttons ── -->
<div class="toggle-wrap">
  <button id="btnEn" class="active" onclick="toggleLang('en')">English</button>
  <button id="btnCn" class="active" onclick="toggleLang('cn')">中文</button>
  <button id="btnBoth" class="active" onclick="toggleLang('both')">Both</button>
</div>

<script>
function toggleLang(mode) {
  document.querySelectorAll('.card.en').forEach(el => {
    el.style.display = (mode === 'en' || mode === 'both') ? '' : 'none';
  });
  document.querySelectorAll('.card.cn').forEach(el => {
    el.style.display = (mode === 'cn' || mode === 'both') ? '' : 'none';
  });
  document.querySelectorAll('.row').forEach(row => {
    if (mode === 'both') {
      row.style.gridTemplateColumns = '1fr 1fr';
    } else {
      row.style.gridTemplateColumns = '1fr';
    }
  });
  document.getElementById('btnEn').classList.toggle('active', mode === 'en');
  document.getElementById('btnCn').classList.toggle('active', mode === 'cn');
  document.getElementById('btnBoth').classList.toggle('active', mode === 'both');
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
"}

